---
id: window
name: Window
kind: type
---
Constructs a window object. Give it a name and select it explicitly with
`windowName.run()`.

### Fields:
 - the declaration name identifies the window object.
 - `title`: the window title.
 - `background`: RGB for the background color formatted as: `R G B`.
 - `width`: an integer value to determine the width of the window.
 - `height`: an integer value to determine the height of the window.
---
id: window.add
name: Window add
kind: method
---
Adds a declared widget object to a window: `my_window.add(my_label);`.

---
id: window.remove
name: Window remove
kind: method
---
Removes a declared widget or trigger from a window: `my_window.remove(my_label);`.
The object declaration remains available, so the same object can be added again.

---
id: window.run
name: Window run
kind: method
---
Selects a window as the program entry point: `my_window.run();`.

---
id: add
name: Add
kind: method
---
Declare widgets as objects, then add them with `windowName.add(widgetName)`.

---
id: label
name: Label
kind: element
---
Creates a non-clickable text widget.

---
id: par
name: Paragraph
kind: element
---
Creates a multiline paragraph text widget with wrapping.

---
id: button
name: Button
kind: element
---
Creates a clickable button widget.

---
id: textbox
name: Textbox
kind: element
---
Creates an editable text input. Read its current contents with `inputId.text`.

---
id: textarea
name: Textarea
kind: element
---
Creates a multiline editable text input. Read its current contents with `inputId.text`.

---
id: rect
name: Rectangle
kind: element
---
Creates a filled rectangle with `x`, `y`, `width`, `height`, and clockwise `angle` in degrees.

---
id: circle
name: Circle
kind: element
---
Creates a filled circle. `x` and `y` specify its center; `radius` defaults to 10.

---
id: triangle
name: Triangle
kind: element
---
Creates a filled triangle from `p1`, `p2`, and `p3` coordinate pairs. Omit all three for an upward equilateral triangle with side length about 10. When supplied with both `x` and `y`, the triangle is placed by its centroid. Its `angle` rotates it clockwise around that centroid.

---
id: placeholder
name: Placeholder
kind: property
---
Text shown in an empty textbox. It disappears when the textbox receives input.

---
id: onclick
name: On Click
kind: block
---
Defines actions that run when a button is clicked.

---
id: update
name: Window Update
kind: method
---
Updates widget or window properties. 

Example:
~~~pxl
greeting.text = "Hello";
greeting.font = ARIAL;
my_window.update();
~~~

Assignments change widget state in memory. Call `my_window.update()` to redraw
the window and commit the changes to the screen.

---
id: title
name: Title
kind: property
---
Sets the window title text.

---
id: iconPath
name: Icon Path
kind: property
---
Sets the path to the application icon.

---
id: width
name: Width
kind: property
---
Sets a window or widget width in pixels.

---
id: height
name: Height
kind: property
---
Sets a window or widget height in pixels.

---
id: font
name: Font
kind: property
---
Sets a widget font. Supported constants include `ARIAL`, `CALIBRI`, `CONSOLAS`, `COURIERNEW`, `TIMESNEWROMAN`, `TAHOMA`, and `VERDANA`.

---
id: fontSize
name: Font Size
kind: property
---
Sets widget text size in pixels.

---
id: angle
name: Angle
kind: property
---
Sets a rectangle or triangle rotation in clockwise degrees.

---
id: radius
name: Radius
kind: property
---
Sets a circle radius. Use `circleId.radius++` or `circleId.radius--` to change it incrementally.

---
id: p1
name: Point 1
kind: property
---
Triangle point one, written as `(x, y)`.

---
id: p2
name: Point 2
kind: property
---
Triangle point two, written as `(x, y)`.

---
id: p3
name: Point 3
kind: property
---
Triangle point three, written as `(x, y)`.

---
id: x
name: X Position
kind: property
---
Sets the horizontal position of a widget.

---
id: y
name: Y Position
kind: property
---
Sets the vertical position of a widget.

---
id: text
name: Text
kind: property
---
Sets the displayed text for a label or button.

---
id: background
name: Background
kind: property
---
Sets an RGB background color. Each channel must be between 0 and 255.

---
id: closeTrigger
name: Close Trigger
kind: trigger
---
Runs the trigger body when the attached window receives a close request.

---
id: int
name: Integer
kind: type
---
Declares a whole-number variable.

---
id: short
name: Short Integer
kind: type
---
Declares a small whole-number variable.

---
id: long
name: Long Integer
kind: type
---
Declares a large whole-number variable.

---
id: float
name: Float
kind: type
---
Declares a single-precision decimal variable.

---
id: double
name: Double
kind: type
---
Declares a double-precision decimal variable.

---
id: bool
name: Boolean
kind: type
---
Declares a `true` or `false` variable.

---
id: char
name: Character
kind: type
---
Declares a single-character variable.

---
id: String
name: String
kind: type
---
Declares a text variable.

---
id: if
name: If
kind: statement
---
Runs a block when a condition is true. Conditions support `&&`, `||`, `!`, comparisons, and parentheses.

---
id: while
name: While
kind: statement
---
Repeats a block while a condition is true. Conditions support `&&`, `||`, `!`, comparisons, and parentheses.

---
id: for
name: For
kind: statement
---
Repeats a block using a numeric initializer, condition, and `++` increment.

---
id: switch_view
name: Switch View
kind: statement
---
Switches to the named window and destroys the current window.

Example: `switch_view(settings);`

---
id: add_view
name: Add View
kind: statement
---
Switches to the named window while keeping the current window open.

Example: `add_view(settings);`

---
id: trigger
name: Trigger
kind: type
---
Create a named trigger object, then attach it to a window with `window.add(trigger)`.

Example: `trigger refresh = trigger (score == 10) { ... }`

## Special Triggers

Condition triggers run every time their condition is true while attached to a
window. `mouseMove` and `onkey("a")` remain available as event conditions.

To set keyboard triggers:

`trigger key = trigger(onkey("a")) { ... }` runs every time the key is pressed.
`trigger close = trigger(closeTrigger) { ... }` runs when the window closes.

---
id: onkey
name: On Key
kind: function
---
Triggers on an exact, case-sensitive key. Named keys include `space`, `esc`, `enter`, `shift`, `alt`, `up`, `down`, `left`, `right`, and `tab`.

---
id: onkeyci
name: On Key (Case Insensitive)
kind: function
---
Triggers on a key without distinguishing upper and lower case.

---
id: mouse
name: Mouse
kind: object
---
Provides `mouse.x` and `mouse.y`, and supports cursor shape updates.

---
id: ARROW
name: Arrow Cursor
kind: constant
---
The standard arrow cursor.

---
id: IBEAM
name: I-Beam Cursor
kind: constant
---
The text-selection cursor.

---
id: WAIT
name: Wait Cursor
kind: constant
---
The busy/wait cursor.

---
id: CROSS
name: Cross Cursor
kind: constant
---
The crosshair cursor.

---
id: UPARROW
name: Up Arrow Cursor
kind: constant
---
The vertical arrow cursor.

---
id: SIZE
name: Resize Cursor
kind: constant
---
The all-direction resize cursor.

---
id: ICON
name: Icon Cursor
kind: constant
---
The legacy icon cursor.

---
id: SIZENWSE
name: Northwest/Southeast Resize Cursor
kind: constant
---
Diagonal resize cursor.

---
id: SIZENESW
name: Northeast/Southwest Resize Cursor
kind: constant
---
Diagonal resize cursor.

---
id: SIZEWE
name: Horizontal Resize Cursor
kind: constant
---
Horizontal resize cursor.

---
id: SIZENS
name: Vertical Resize Cursor
kind: constant
---
Vertical resize cursor.

---
id: SIZEALL
name: Move Cursor
kind: constant
---
Move cursor.

---
id: NO
name: Unavailable Cursor
kind: constant
---
The unavailable cursor.

---
id: HAND
name: Hand Cursor
kind: constant
---
The hand cursor.

---
id: APPSTARTING
name: App Starting Cursor
kind: constant
---
The arrow-plus-busy cursor.

---
id: HELP
name: Help Cursor
kind: constant
---
The help cursor.

---
id: PIN
name: Pin Cursor
kind: constant
---
The pin cursor when supported by Windows.

---
id: PERSON
name: Person Cursor
kind: constant
---
The person cursor when supported by Windows.
